title: Internal Security
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
on-arrival: police_timer += 6; month_actions += 1
view-if: CHP_in_government = 1 and interior_minister_party = "CHP" and police_timer <= 0
card-image: img/portraits/necdetugur2.png

= Internal Security

The Interior Ministry controls internal security throughout the Turkish Republic.

- @loyalty: Improve the loyalty of the Interior Ministry forces.
- @recruit: Recruit more police forces.
- @weaponry: Supplement the weaponry and the strength of the police forces.
- @investigate_corruption: Investigate corruption by big businesses.
- @investigate_far_right: Investigate illegal activity among the far right.
- @investigate_separatists: Investigate illegal activity among separatists.
- @easterncrime: Strike against the drug smugglers and organized crime along the Southeastern Border.
- @ohal: Declare OHAL(state of emergency) to put an end to the street fighting.
- @root: Take no action for now.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@loyalty
on-arrival: {! Q.police_loyalty=Math.min(1,AnatolianRules.number(Q.police_loyalty)+0.2); !}

There are measures we can take to unveil the ideological cliques, prioritizing the advancement of their ideology to the wellbeing of the state, within the police forces. We can improve training and recruiting procedures, and identify and remove known extremists and the like.

Current interior police loyalty: [+ police_loyalty : loyalty +]

@recruit
on-arrival: police_strength += 16; police_loyalty -= 0.05

The new police regiments strengthen the state's hold over the streets, though we have received reports of a decrease in general loyalty.

@weaponry
subtitle: -1 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough budget.
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; {! Q.police_militancy=Math.min(1,AnatolianRules.number(Q.police_militancy)+0.2); !}

The police forces have been supplemented with better weapons and training, improving their efficiency.

@investigate_corruption
go-to: investigate_corruption_success if police_loyalty >= 0.5; investigate_corruption_failure if police_loyalty < 0.5

@investigate_corruption_success
on-arrival: investigate_corruption += 1; workers_chp += 5*(1-dissent); inflation_modifier -= 0.1 if inflation > 3; inflation_modifier -= 0.2 if inflation >= 8; {! AnatolianRules.refreshEconomy(Q); !}

Corruption in big business is rampant, of course. We have uncovered a number of scandals, and publicizing them brings new attention to the work of Interior Minister [+ interior_minister +], building up his popular appeal and that of the CHP.


@investigate_corruption_failure

Unfortunately, our investigations have failed to turn up anything. Rumors are that the targets of our investigation were tipped off by infiltrators within the police.

@investigate_far_right
new-page: true

= Investigate illegal activity among the far right

The ministry can act against armed organizations and investigate the anti-communist underground. Initial bans require far-right strength to reach at least 35%. A ban disrupts recruitment and weapons networks, but does not end the organization. Further prosecutions remove up to twenty thousand members and slightly reduce militarization.

- @ban_grey: Ban the Grey Wolves.
- @ban_raiders: Ban the Raiders.
- @investigate_tit: Investigate the Revenge Brigades.
- @pursue_grey: Further Persecute Grey Wolves.
- @pursue_raiders: Further Persecute Raiders.
- @pursue_tit: Persecute the Revenge Brigades.
- @underground: Investigate Far Right and Anti-Communist Underground.
- @clamp_ohp: Clamp down on ÖHP.
- @root: Take no further action.

@ban_grey
view-if: not grey_wolves_banned
choose-if: far_right_force_percent >= 35
unavailable-subtitle: Far-right strength must reach at least 35%.
on-arrival: {! AnatolianRules.securityAction(Q,'grey_wolves',true); !}

The Grey Wolves are banned. Recruitment and organization are disrupted: their membership falls by 40% and militarization by 35%. The network survives underground and requires further action.

- @root: Continue.

@ban_raiders
view-if: not raiders_banned and raiders_formed == 1
choose-if: far_right_force_percent >= 35
unavailable-subtitle: Far-right strength must reach at least 35%.
on-arrival: {! AnatolianRules.securityAction(Q,'raiders',true); !}

The Raiders are banned. Recruitment and organization are disrupted: their membership falls by 40% and militarization by 35%. The network survives underground and requires further action.

- @root: Continue.

@investigate_tit
view-if: not tit_investigated
choose-if: true
unavailable-subtitle: There are no active members left to prosecute.
on-arrival: {! AnatolianRules.securityAction(Q,'tit',true); !}

Investigators identify the Revenge Brigades’ clandestine structures and gather evidence. The ministry can now prosecute their members and disrupt their weapons networks.

- @root: Continue.

@pursue_grey
view-if: grey_wolves_banned == 1
choose-if: {! return AnatolianRules.number(Q.grey_wolves_strength)>0; !}
unavailable-subtitle: There are no active members left to prosecute.
on-arrival: {! AnatolianRules.securityAction(Q,'grey_wolves',false); !}

Further prosecutions of the Grey Wolves remove up to twenty thousand members from the active pool. Weapons seizures reduce militarization by 0.03. Surviving networks may still recruit again.

- @root: Continue.

@pursue_raiders
view-if: raiders_banned == 1 and raiders_formed == 1
choose-if: {! return AnatolianRules.number(Q.raiders_strength)>0; !}
unavailable-subtitle: There are no active members left to prosecute.
on-arrival: {! AnatolianRules.securityAction(Q,'raiders',false); !}

Further prosecutions of the Raiders remove up to twenty thousand members from the active pool. Weapons seizures reduce militarization by 0.03. Surviving networks may still recruit again.

- @root: Continue.

@pursue_tit
view-if: tit_investigated == 1
choose-if: {! return AnatolianRules.number(Q.tit_strength)>0; !}
unavailable-subtitle: There are no active members left to prosecute.
on-arrival: {! AnatolianRules.securityAction(Q,'tit',false); !}

Further prosecutions of the Revenge Brigades remove up to twenty thousand members from the active pool. Weapons seizures reduce militarization by 0.03. Surviving networks may still recruit again.

- @root: Continue.

@underground
view-if: {! return AnatolianRules.number(Q.ohp_investigations)<4; !}
on-arrival: {! AnatolianRules.investigateUnderground(Q); !}
new-page: true

= The anti-communist underground

[? if ohp_investigations == 1 : Investigators find that several far-right groups have access to weapons and contacts beyond their public organizations. Reports refer to a Counter-Guerrilla network, but the chains of command remain concealed. ?]
[? if ohp_investigations == 2 : The inquiry traces contacts to secret stay-behind preparations within the Cold War alliance. Similar networks abroad are associated with Operation Gladio. The ministry has identified connections, but does not yet know enough to intervene effectively. ?]
[? if ohp_investigations == 3 : Records point towards Özel Harp Dairesi, the Special Warfare Department under the General Staff. Its official purpose is resistance against an occupation, but the investigation finds indications of domestic political activity outside proper civilian oversight. ?]
[? if ohp_investigations >= 4 : The government now understands the department’s hidden funding arrangements and the underground networks linked to it. The inquiry has gathered enough evidence to restrict clandestine support and impose civilian scrutiny. The department cannot be eliminated by a single decision, but its capacity can be weakened. ?]

- @root: Continue.

@clamp_ohp
view-if: ohp_investigations >= 4
choose-if: {! return AnatolianRules.ohpClampAvailable(Q); !}
unavailable-subtitle: ÖHP is already at its residual strength, or its embargo-related funding request must first be addressed.
on-arrival: {! AnatolianRules.clampOHP(Q); !}

Civilian oversight and restrictions on hidden funding weaken ÖHP. Its strength falls by twenty percentage points, slowing the growth of far-right paramilitary groups. A residual network remains beyond our ability to dismantle fully.

- @root: Continue.

@investigate_separatists
go-to: investigate_separatists_success if police_loyalty >= 0.55 and pkk_formed; investigate_separatists_failure if police_loyalty < 0.55 or not pkk_formed

@investigate_separatists_success
on-arrival: pkk_strength *= 0.7; pkk_militancy -= 0.05

We have struck against PKK cells and confiscated their weapon caches, disrupting their operations.

@investigate_separatists_failure

Our attempts to find separatist militants have failed, and our informants report that leaks may have warned them.

@easterncrime
choose-if: police_loyalty >= 0.50 and police_force >= 55 and eastern_crime > 0
subtitle: The economic problems, largely due to the huge rates of crime and smuggling, in the East constitute a significant factor in the rise of Kurdish Nationalism.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if police_loyalty <= 0.49 : Our police forces are too disorganized and unloyal for such operations. ?][? if police_force <= 54 : Our police forces aren't strong enough to enforce the law against organized crime in the East! ?][? if eastern_crime < 0 : Large scale crime has already been exterminated in the East. ?]
on-arrival: police_militancy -= 0.08; eastern_crime -= 1; kurds_chp += 3

[? if eastern_crime >= 4 : We have raided some drug depots in the border regions, however more work is needed to solve the issue altogether. ?]
[? if eastern_crime = 3 : Continuous raids and operations in the East have begun weakening the power of the local gangs! ?]
[? if eastern_crime = 2 : The crime rates have been decreased significantly thanks to the determination of the security forces. ?]
[? if eastern_crime = 1 : The region has largely been neutralized, with only isolated incidents remaining as remnants of past instability. ?]
[? if eastern_crime = 0 : The region has been completely neutralized; the region at last enjoys lasting order and stability. Many are grateful to our party for ending the lawlessness which has persisted for centuries. ?]

@ohal
choose-if: OHAL = 0 and state_force_percent <= 49 or year >= 1978
subtitle: Though a drastic move and something we are ideologically opposed to, we may be forced to declare a state of emergency and and restrict the civil rights in order to bring peace to the streets.
unavailable-subtitle: The situation in the streets still can be managed through conventional means.
on-arrival: grey_wolves_militancy -= 0.1; grey_wolves_strength -= 8; devyol_militancy -= 0.1; devyol_strength -= 8; raiders_strength -= 8; workers_chp -= 5; rural_chp -= 3; state_employees_chp -= 3; petty_bourgeoisie_chp -= 3; kurds_chp -= 3; alevis_chp -= 3; OHAL += 1

Our voters are deeply irritated by our decision to initiate the militarization of the streets when we were the party promising to stop it. Ecevit's persona as the uncorrupted fighter for democracy breaks down as we resort to pragmatic actions we normally despise. However, hopefully this will be worth it for the motherland.
